<!--
  Extra Info.plist entries for the Rylus.app bundle, injected by cargo-bundle
  via `osx_info_plist_exts` (see crates/rylus-server/Cargo.toml).

  cargo-bundle reads this file's raw contents and appends them verbatim into
  the generated Info.plist's top-level <dict>, before closing </dict></plist>.
  It must therefore contain bare <key>/<value> pairs, not a full plist
  document (no <?xml ...?>, <!DOCTYPE ...>, or <plist>/<dict> wrapper).

  These are the macOS TCC (Transparency, Consent, and Control) usage-
  description strings shown to the user in the permission prompt:

  - NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription: required for Rylus to capture the
    display via ScreenCaptureKit/CGDisplayStream.
  - NSAppleEventsUsageDescription: required if Rylus sends Apple Events
    (e.g. for AppleScript-driven input injection / automation hooks).
-->
<key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
<string>Rylus needs Screen Recording access to capture your display and share it with your stylus/tablet client.</string>
<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
<string>Rylus needs Apple Events access to inject stylus and keyboard input into other applications.</string>
